## Summary (non-binding — see full text for the actual terms)

AGPL-3.0 grants you the freedom to:

- Use the software for any purpose
- Study and modify the source code
- Distribute copies
- Improve and redistribute your improvements
- Use the software in your own SaaS — **provided you publish your complete
  source code under AGPL-3.0** to your users (this is the "Affero" part,
  designed to prevent closed-source SaaS forks)

Under AGPL-3.0 you **must**:

- Keep the copyright notice intact
- License your modifications under AGPL-3.0
- Provide source code to anyone you distribute binaries to
- **If you run a modified version as a network service, you must release
  the complete corresponding source code to them.**

If you do not wish to release your source code under AGPL-3.0 — for example,
because you are building a closed-source SaaS product that incorporates this
software — you must obtain a commercial license from us. See LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md
for details and pricing.

---

## Why dual-license?

We believe open-source is the right default for the quant-trading community:

- Independent researchers and individual quants should be able to read, run,
  and modify the code without a paywall.
- Academic study of trading AI behavior should be free.
- Community contributions improve quality for everyone.

We also believe the team that builds the system should be paid:

- A commercial license is required if you want to embed Reflex Quant in a
  closed-source product, white-label it, or resell it without publishing your
  modifications.
- Commercial licensing revenue funds continued open-source development.

If you're not sure which license applies to your situation, email us:
z2132743607@163.com

